data.hypothesis:
The pulse sits at the k2/k3 interface and both ends are absorbing. The prior-averaged local CRB, sigma^2 diag(H^{-1}), is therefore smaller for k2 and k3 than for k1 and k4. Because the right-hand sensors are one cell farther from the pulse and nearer the boundary, CRB_k4 >= CRB_k1 and CRB_k3 >= CRB_k2.

An MLP on log features with log-k targets and no extra augmentation then satisfies:
(a) val rel_l2 < 0.05;
(b) max(err_k2, err_k3) < min(err_k1, err_k4) < 0.25;
(c) the same inner < outer ordering appears in the local CRB from P-011's Hessians.

Secondary: err_k4 >= err_k1 and err_k3 >= err_k2.

